{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.g3_ratio_im_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.g3_ratio_im_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L134-L142","doc":"**Conditional on `SharedConjugationCovariance`:** the 5₂ ratio is real,\n`(I_FW τ / Z_GGM τ).im = 0`. This is the structural theorem behind the 1e-32\nnumerical G3 match — realness from the shared conjugation symmetry, with NO\nfloat bound in the proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.g3_ratio_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.g3_ratio_real","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L125-L132","doc":"**Conditional on `SharedConjugationCovariance`:** `star (I_FW τ / Z_GGM τ)\n= I_FW τ / Z_GGM τ` — the 5₂ ratio is fixed by conjugation. Fully verified by\nLean modulo the single class-axiomatised covariance input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.SharedConjugationCovariance.shared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.SharedConjugationCovariance.shared","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L122-L122","doc":"For each `τ`, a common nonzero conjugation factor `u` covariates both\nintegrals. The existential packages the (data) phase `u` inside a `Prop`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.SharedConjugationCovariance.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.SharedConjugationCovariance.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.SharedConjugationCovariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.SharedConjugationCovariance","kind":"class","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L108-L123","doc":"**OPEN hypothesis (conditional class).** The Fantini–Wheeler combination\n`I_FW` and the Garoufalidis–Gu–Mariño assembly `Z_GGM` of the 5₂ state integral\nare conjugation-covariant with a *common* law: for each `τ` there is a nonzero\n`u` (a phase, rooted in the saddle conjugate-pairing `V₂ = conj V₁`) with\n`conj (I_FW τ) = u * I_FW τ` and `conj (Z_GGM τ) = u * Z_GGM τ`.\n\nNOT proved. The 5₂ AK-integral probe (PR #4475) found `Im(I_FW/Z_GGM) ≈ 1e-32`\n— that numeric is EVIDENCE for this covariance, not a proof of it. A proof would\nfollow from FW Thm 1.4 (bean `qou-h7yk`) plus the established saddle\nconjugate-pairing. Held as a `[SharedConjugationCovariance]` hypothesis so the\ndownstream realness result is an honest §3b-cond conditional theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.ratio_im_zero_of_shared_law","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.ratio_im_zero_of_shared_law","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L86-L98","doc":"**Shared conjugation law ⇒ the ratio is real** (`(a / b).im = 0`).\n\nThe `ℂ` specialisation of `ratio_star_fixed_of_shared_law`: a complex number\nfixed by conjugation has zero imaginary part. This is the honest content of the\nnumerical `Im(I_FW/Z_GGM) ≈ 1e-32` — realness follows from the SYMMETRY, not\nfrom the float bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.ratio_star_fixed_of_shared_law","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.G3RealnessConjugationBrick.ratio_star_fixed_of_shared_law","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/G3RealnessConjugationBrick.lean#L65-L80","doc":"**Shared conjugation law ⇒ the ratio is a fixed point of the star map.**\n\nIf `star a = u * a` and `star b = u * b` for a common NONZERO `u`, then the\nunit `u` cancels in `a / b`, so `star (a / b) = a / b`.\n\nThis is genuine algebraic content, not a tautology: it is FALSE without the\nshared-`u` hypothesis (e.g. `star a = u * a`, `star b = v * b` with `u ≠ v`\ngives `star (a/b) = (u/v)·(a/b) ≠ a/b` in general). Holds in any field with a\nstar ring structure; `ℂ` is not required. ","signatureChunk":0}]}